<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_SlimeVisitorSeed.xml              §10, owner ruling 2026-09-24 ("Yes, I
  think that's a good idea" to BENCH's offer of a visitor seed pass).

  Runs once, at generation, on any newly generated RM_GelatinousSlime map:
  spawns 3-5 never-hostile arrivals drawn from the neighbouring world tiles'
  own wildAnimals (same read MapComponent_SlimeVisitors.BuildNeighbourRoster
  uses for the ambient trickle), each carrying Slimification at the standard
  arrival severity (0.25-0.7), so the biome opens already showing
  "everything that ever touched it" instead of gelatids-only for the first
  days.

  Order 751: right after Core's own wildlife step (750) — after terrain,
  roads and the biome's native wildAnimals have placed their pawns, so this
  reads as part of the same population wave and MaxVisitorsOnMap's cap sees
  an accurate count — and long before anything that matters to a fresh
  landing (colonist placement, item scatter). Generate() below self-gates on
  map.Biome, so registering it globally (below) is safe: it no-ops on every
  non-Slime map, the same shape RM_GenStep_LiquidShores/
  RUT_FungalSoilScatter already use.
-->
<Defs>

  <GenStepDef>
    <defName>RM_SlimeVisitorSeed</defName>
    <order>751</order>
    <genStep Class="RimMandrake.GelatinousSlime.GenStep_SlimeVisitorSeed" />
  </GenStepDef>

</Defs>
